 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Score-based Densification](4705-score-based-densification.md)
-Score-based Densification is a constructive densification strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting that steers the addition of new primitives toward those that maximize reconstruction quality, ensuring the model size increases in a controlled manner toward an exact user-defined budget. Unlike standard adaptive density control which relies on gradient thresholds and subsequent pruning, this method uses a purely constructive schedule, avoiding the optimization instability and hardware constraint violations caused by substantial pruning or culling during training.
