 ### [GroupFlow](6351-groupflow.md)
-GroupFlow is a motion compression technique for dynamic 3D Gaussian Splatting that distills per-Gaussian neural deformation fields into shared SE(3) transformations for groupwise motion. It solves the computational bottleneck of evaluating individual deformation networks for every Gaussian at every timestep by clustering Gaussians into groups and assigning each group a single learned rigid-body trajectory. Unlike methods that retain per-Gaussian neural fields or use global rigid transforms, GroupFlow captures locally coherent motion with $J \ll N$ parameters, accelerating rendering by up to 13.71× while maintaining temporal coherence.
