 ### [VS-Splat Voxel Selection](9132-vs-splat-voxel-selection.md)
-VS-Splat voxel selection is a learnable, differentiable mechanism for filtering 3D Gaussian primitives based on their relevance to the target object, replacing static opacity thresholding. It solves the problem of background noise and redundant primitives in sparse-view reconstruction by predicting confidence scores via Gumbel-Sigmoid and using them to refine opacity values. It sets itself apart from siblings like [Score-based Densification](4705-score-based-densification.md) by operating on a voxel grid with learned confidence rather than gradient norms, and from [Adaptive Density Control](9188-adaptive-density-control.md) by using a stochastic binary approximation for selection rather than deterministic splitting rules.
