 ### [Opacity Split for Cloning](9694-opacity-split-for-cloning.md)
-Opacity Split for Cloning is a method to initialize the opacity of cloned Gaussians to maintain transmittance consistency, preventing the cloned child from having less impact than the parent alone. It solves the problem where standard cloning inherits the parent's full opacity, which artificially increases the total transmittance attenuation of the parent-child pair compared to the original single Gaussian, thereby biasing the alpha blending process. It sets itself apart from generic cloning by explicitly deriving new opacity values from the parent's opacity to preserve the cumulative transmittance $t_k$ before and after the split.
