 ### [Hybrid and Diffusion Representations](11473-hybrid-and-diffusion-representations.md)
-Hybrid and Diffusion Representations extend 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) from a discriminative reconstruction technique to a generative framework, enabling scene synthesis from single images or text prompts without iterative per-scene optimization. Unlike standard differentiable training loops that optimize Gaussian parameters via gradient descent to fit observed views, these methods employ feed-forward networks or diffusion models to directly predict Gaussian attributes. This approach solves the latency bottleneck of inverse rendering while addressing generation-specific artifacts such as the "Janus problem" (geometric inconsistency across viewpoints) and "floaters" (spurious low-opacity primitives).
